WEBVTT

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:09.371
Welcome to the second
part of this tutorial, where we

00:00:09.372 --> 00:00:12.930
will focus on the data analysis
using the software Jamobi.

00:00:14.239 --> 00:00:16.225
Before starting, it is
essential to remember that

00:00:16.226 --> 00:00:19.570
we must already have built
our form in Google Forms.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:23.610
To advance with the analysis, it is
necessary that this form has already been

00:00:23.611 --> 00:00:27.350
completed by organizations or people with
whom we previously shared the link.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.470
Step 1.

00:00:29.835 --> 00:00:30.835
Access the data.

00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:34.850
The first thing we will do will be to
enter our email account.

00:00:35.439 --> 00:00:39.270
Go to the application menu, the icon of
the points in the upper right corner,

00:00:40.059 --> 00:00:41.450
and select Forms.

00:00:42.519 --> 00:00:45.310
Once there, open the form that you
previously created.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:47.350
Step 2.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:48.490
Check the answers.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.014
In the upper part of
the screen there will be

00:00:51.015 --> 00:00:53.110
three tabs, questions,
answers and configuration.

00:00:53.775 --> 00:00:54.970
We will click on answers.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.190
Here you can see the total
number of participation

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.330
and a brief summary
of the collected data.

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:02.310
Step 3.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.090
Export the spreadsheet.

00:01:04.609 --> 00:01:08.310
To work with these data, select the option
to see in the spreadsheet.

00:01:09.659 --> 00:01:12.819
This will allow you to access the information
in a format compatible with Excel.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.410
Step 4.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.330
Understand the structure of the data.

00:01:16.839 --> 00:01:19.119
When you open the spreadsheet,
you will see the following.

00:01:20.049 --> 00:01:22.810
In the rows, we will find the numbers of
each answer.

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:26.752
In statistics, this is known
as the number of cases that

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:29.290
represents each time that an
organization completed the form.

00:01:30.199 --> 00:01:32.510
In the columns, we will see the questions
we made.

00:01:33.509 --> 00:01:37.270
Each of these columns represents a
variable, which is the specific

00:01:37.271 --> 00:01:39.511
information that we want to analyze of
each organization.

00:01:40.769 --> 00:01:44.050
Continuing with the process, once the
application Yamobi is installed,

00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:48.930
we look for the icon in our office or
application menu and we open it.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:50.730
Step 1.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:52.030
Main interface.

00:01:52.364 --> 00:01:55.084
When entering, you will find
a very similar grid interface

00:01:55.085 --> 00:01:58.170
to the one of Excel, organized
by rows and columns.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:02.150
This is the space where we will register
the collected information of the

00:02:02.151 --> 00:02:04.650
organizations or members that answered our
form.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.170
Step 2.

00:02:08.169 --> 00:02:09.169
Variable configuration.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.297
It is very important to
correctly configure the

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.650
columns, which represent
our questions or categories.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.486
When accessing the
configuration of a column, the

00:02:18.487 --> 00:02:20.647
first thing we must define
is the name of the variable.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.643
It is recommended to use
short names and avoid special

00:02:23.644 --> 00:02:26.350
characters to facilitate the
processing of data in the software.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:28.230
Step 3.

00:02:28.694 --> 00:02:30.054
Definition of the type of measure.

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:35.210
The next key point is the type of measure,
which directly depends on the nature of

00:02:35.211 --> 00:02:36.990
the question and its categories of
response.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.388
Although the program
offers several options, we

00:02:40.389 --> 00:02:42.910
will focus on the three
main ones for our analysis.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:44.610
Nominal.

00:02:45.054 --> 00:02:48.290
It is used for variables, whose categories
do not have a hierarchy order.

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:50.890
For example, names or types of
organization.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.050
Ordinal.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:56.490
It is applied when the categories do
follow a specific or hierarchical order.

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:57.930
Continuous.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:01.189
It is the option for numerical
variables, used when the answer

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:03.870
is a number or a measure,
like the extension in kilometers.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.252
A fundamental point
that we must consider is

00:03:08.253 --> 00:03:10.013
the handling of multiple
selection questions.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:14.440
In our form, these are
the questions that allow

00:03:14.441 --> 00:03:16.510
users to mark several
options simultaneously.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.150
It is important to note how these data
appear in the Google spreadsheet.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:25.490
You will observe that all the answers
selected by the same organization are

00:03:25.491 --> 00:03:28.310
grouped in a single cell, separated simply
by comma.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:33.870
Identifying this format is key before
taking the data to Yamobi, since it will

00:03:33.871 --> 00:03:37.510
require a special treatment so that each
option can be analyzed as an independent

00:03:37.511 --> 00:03:40.617
variable, unlike the
unique selection questions,

00:03:40.618 --> 00:03:42.930
where the user only
chooses one option.

00:03:43.495 --> 00:03:46.335
In this case, it is not necessary to
create or add additional variables.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.870
With these clear precisions, it is time to
start building our database in Yamobi.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:56.076
Step 1.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.910
Identify the data in the Google
spreadsheet.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:02.630
First, we will open our spreadsheet with
the answers of the form.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:08.070
For this example, we will work with three
questions, starting with the first one.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:10.595
What is the name of the organization?

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:16.209
You will see that this question heads the
column, while the rows, from the number,

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:18.649
number 2, contain the answers of each
organization.

00:04:19.205 --> 00:04:21.070
In total, we have 8 cases.

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:23.290
Step 2.

00:04:23.615 --> 00:04:24.970
Configure the variable in Yamobi.

00:04:25.575 --> 00:04:28.500
Now, in the Yamobi interface,
we will double-click on

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:32.370
the letter A in the top corner
to configure the column.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:37.250
Instead of writing the full question as
the name of the variable, we will use a

00:04:37.251 --> 00:04:39.887
short and descriptive
name, as the name of

00:04:39.888 --> 00:04:42.370
the organization to
facilitate the analysis.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:44.690
Step 3.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:46.250
Define measure and description.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.290
Next, we will define the type of measure.

00:04:49.835 --> 00:04:52.770
When we deal with names of organizations
that do not have a hierarchical order

00:04:52.771 --> 00:04:55.170
between them, we will select the nominal
option.

00:04:56.265 --> 00:04:59.590
In the description field, here we can
write the full question.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.190
What is the name of the organization?

00:05:02.805 --> 00:05:05.650
Which will serve us as a visual guide
within the database?

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:07.850
Step 4.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:09.986
Data load.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.427
Finally, we are located
in the first row to

00:05:12.428 --> 00:05:14.530
enter the answers of
the Google spreadsheet.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:16.650
You can do it manually.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:22.410
Or, for greater quickness, simply copy the
data of the spreadsheet, right-click and

00:05:22.411 --> 00:05:26.070
copy, and paste them directly in the
corresponding column of Yamobi.

00:05:26.245 --> 00:05:29.590
Make sure that, for this exercise, the
eight cases have been imported correctly.

00:05:34.395 --> 00:05:37.080
We continue to feed our database in
Yamobi.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:39.980
Now we will proceed with question number
2.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:41.880
Step 1.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.140
Location of the data.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:48.080
We return to our Google spreadsheet to
locate the next column.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:52.456
The question is, what
is the legal nature or

00:05:52.457 --> 00:05:54.620
status of recognition
of its organization?

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:59.860
It is advisable to verify in the original
form that the question coincides and

00:05:59.861 --> 00:06:05.280
remember that, in this case, it is a
single question with four answers.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:07.360
Step 2.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.040
Configuration in Yamobi.

00:06:10.065 --> 00:06:15.300
Now, in Yamobi, we go to column B and
double-click to configure it.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:20.340
We will assign a simplified name for the
variable, such as natural nature under legal.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.760
Just like in the previous case,
the type of measure must be nominal,

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.600
since the categories do not have a
hierarchical order.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:29.560
Step 3.

00:06:29.705 --> 00:06:31.400
Description and data load.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.412
In the description field,
we will paste the full

00:06:36.413 --> 00:06:38.720
question of the form to
facilitate our reference.

00:06:40.065 --> 00:06:43.440
Once configured to the column,
we must transfer the answers, ensuring

00:06:43.441 --> 00:06:45.601
that they coincide with the corresponding
organization.

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:50.720
You can copy all the answers from the
spreadsheet and paste them in Yamobi,

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:52.140
or enter them manually.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:01.090
By finishing the
registration of the second

00:07:01.091 --> 00:07:03.520
question, we will move
on to question number 3.

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:08.100
This step is crucial, since it requires a
special treatment in Yamobi.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:10.580
Step 1.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:14.860
If we check our Google spreadsheet,
we will notice that in the questions of

00:07:14.861 --> 00:07:19.220
multiple selection, such as the actions of
defense of the territory, the answers

00:07:19.221 --> 00:07:22.600
appear grouped in a single cell and
separated by commas.

00:07:23.305 --> 00:07:26.503
For example, an organization
may have marked land

00:07:26.504 --> 00:07:30.180
recovery and community
vigilance at the same time.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:35.620
Since Yamobi cannot analyze these options
if they are together in a single column,

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:38.030
we must transform them into independent
variables.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:39.560
Step 2.

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:41.720
Creation of multiple variables.

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:46.860
Instead of creating a single column for
the question, we will create a column for

00:07:46.861 --> 00:07:48.740
each option of available response in the
form.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:54.560
In our example, we will configure four
types of variables, nominal in column C,

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:58.776
we will create the
variable land recovery in

00:07:58.777 --> 00:08:01.380
column D, we will
create place protection.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.150
In the next column, column E, we will
create community vigilance.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:32.740
And finally, in column F, action
megaprojects.

00:08:43.049 --> 00:08:44.049
Step 3.

00:08:44.579 --> 00:08:45.859
How do we enter the information?

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:47.490
It is very simple.

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:50.979
We return to our Google
spreadsheet and verify

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:52.610
which options each
organization selected.

00:08:53.249 --> 00:08:58.790
If the organization marked an option, we
write yes in the corresponding box in Yamobi.

00:08:59.869 --> 00:09:03.470
If the option was not selected,
we write no.

00:09:27.875 --> 00:09:31.850
In this way, a single question of the form
becomes four different variables,

00:09:32.449 --> 00:09:35.239
allowing us to make a
more precise statistical

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.120
analysis for each action
of territorial defense.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:38.890
Perfect.

00:09:39.169 --> 00:09:42.750
Once we have finished assigning the
answers of our three questions of example,

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:47.150
ensuring that we have the eight registered
cases and the variables correctly

00:09:47.151 --> 00:09:50.410
configured, including the special
treatment of multiple options.

00:09:51.869 --> 00:09:53.690
The next step is to secure our work.

00:09:54.549 --> 00:09:58.350
So that we can access this information in
the future and continue to feed the

00:09:58.351 --> 00:10:00.710
database with new data from our Google
form.

00:10:01.829 --> 00:10:02.989
We will continue these steps.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:06.768
Go to the upper left side
of the Yamobi interface,

00:10:06.769 --> 00:10:09.190
where the main menu is
represented by the three rows.

00:10:10.859 --> 00:10:12.610
Select the option Save as.

00:10:13.339 --> 00:10:17.230
In the upper part of the window that is
displayed, change the name of the file by

00:10:17.579 --> 00:10:18.590
map or organization.

00:10:19.319 --> 00:10:21.690
Click on the button Save and ready.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.116
We already have our
database saved and prepared

00:10:24.117 --> 00:10:27.890
to be consulted or updated
at any time we need it.

00:10:27.989 --> 00:10:30.951
This file now contains all
the structure of variables and

00:10:30.952 --> 00:10:33.650
cases that we have carefully
processed from the spreadsheet.